#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDEALIZED TEACHING STRUCTURE -- bundled with ADVISOR as an offline "Try an
# example" starting point. This is NOT a specific experimental deposit and
# carries no COD/ICSD database code or DOI: fabricating one would misrepresent
# its provenance.
#
# Values used, and why:
#   - Rock-salt (NaCl-type) arrangement, space group Fm-3m (No. 225).
#   - Cubic lattice constant a = 5.6402 Angstrom: a commonly cited value for
#     ambient rock salt in standard reference tables (e.g. Wyckoff, Crystal
#     Structures). Chosen for a recognizable, well-behaved example, not
#     measured for this file.
#   - All 8 atoms of the conventional cell are listed explicitly (4x Na on
#     the 4a Wyckoff position, 4x Cl on 4b) rather than relying on a
#     symmetry-operator loop, so no symmetry-expansion step is required to
#     obtain a chemically sensible structure.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data_idealized_rock_salt
_chemical_name_common              'Idealized rock salt (NaCl-type), illustrative'
_chemical_formula_sum              'Na4 Cl4'
_space_group_IT_number             225
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M     'F m -3 m'
_symmetry_cell_setting             cubic
_cell_length_a                     5.6402
_cell_length_b                     5.6402
_cell_length_c                     5.6402
_cell_angle_alpha                  90.0
_cell_angle_beta                   90.0
_cell_angle_gamma                  90.0
_cell_formula_units_Z              4
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
_atom_site_occupancy
Na1 Na 0.0 0.0 0.0 1.0
Na2 Na 0.0 0.5 0.5 1.0
Na3 Na 0.5 0.0 0.5 1.0
Na4 Na 0.5 0.5 0.0 1.0
Cl1 Cl 0.5 0.5 0.5 1.0
Cl2 Cl 0.5 0.0 0.0 1.0
Cl3 Cl 0.0 0.5 0.0 1.0
Cl4 Cl 0.0 0.0 0.5 1.0
